menu "data_matrix"

    config DATA_MATRIX_ROLES
        int "Roles"
        default 8
        range 2 32
        help
          Providers with a role: the ones with a session, a raw port or a
          command port.

    config DATA_MATRIX_ROUTES
        int "Routes"
        default 24
        range 4 128
        help
          Routes of every kind. A delivery copies the routes it takes onto
          its task's stack (3 bytes each).

    config DATA_MATRIX_CALLBACKS
        int "Callbacks"
        default 6
        range 1 16
        help
          Callback ends of the board's code (the watches, the remote devices,
          a module that takes a stream).

    config DATA_MATRIX_QUEUE_SIZE
        int "Queue (bytes)"
        default 4608
        range 1024 32768
        help
          Ring buffer of the messages waiting for the matrix's task: sends on
          streams, and what a route puts into a stream. Each takes its length
          + ~12 bytes, and the one being delivered keeps its room until every
          target has it. A full queue drops it. Multiple of 4.

    config DATA_MATRIX_TASK_PRIO
        int "Task priority"
        default 4
        range 1 24
        help
          Below the router tasks: streams wait, commands don't.

    config DATA_MATRIX_TASK_STACK
        int "Task stack (bytes)"
        default 4096
        range 2048 32768
        help
          Delivering a queued message to its targets, and the callbacks it
          calls.

endmenu
